s"," is omitted (it's not a persisted event).",[318,1318,1320],{"id":1319},"signature-scheme","Signature scheme",[749,1322,1327],{"className":1323,"code":1325,"language":1326},[1324],"language-text","Vatly-Signature: t=1700000000,v1=\u003Chex_hmac_sha256>\nVatly-Event-Id:  webhook_event_Qk8pRtSvWm2NjLhYcZaE\n","text",[326,1328,1325],{"__ignoreMap":754},[1330,1331,1332,1339,1349,1359],"ul",{},[1333,1334,1335,1338],"li",{},[326,1336,1337],{},"t"," is unix seconds, captured fresh on each delivery attempt.",[1333,1340,1341,1344,1345,1348],{},[326,1342,1343],{},"v1"," is ",[326,1346,1347],{},"HMAC-SHA256(\"{t}.{rawBody}\", webhookSecret)",", lowercase hex.",[1333,1350,1351,1352,1355,1356,337],{},"The SDK rejects signatures where ",[326,1353,1354],{},"|now − t| > 300"," seconds by default\n(5-minute clock-skew tolerance). Tune it with ",[326,1357,1358],{},"{ toleranceSeconds }",[1333,1360,1361,1362,1365],{},"Future algorithm rotation ships ",[326,1363,1364],{},"v1=…,v2=…"," simultaneously; the SDK verifies\nany version it recognizes and ignores the rest.",[318,1367,1369],{"id":1368},"deduplication-is-your-job","Deduplication is your job",[293,1371,1372,1373,1376,1377,1379],{},"The SDK is stateless — it can't remember which events it has verified. The\nclock-skew check bounds how long a leaked signature is replayable, but does not\nstop replays inside that window. For full replay defense, dedupe on the\nretry-stable, signed ",[326,1374,1375],{},"event.id"," in your own store after verification. The\n",[326,1378,1299],{}," header is not signed and is for correlation only:",[749,1381,1383],{"className":751,"code":1382,"language":753,"meta":754,"style":754},"const event = await constructWebhookEventFromRequest(request, secret);\nconst eventId = event.id;\nif (await store.has(eventId)) return new Response(\"ok\"); \u002F\u002F already processed\n",[326,1384,1385,1410,1428],{"__ignoreMap":754},[758,1386,1387,1390,1393,1396,1398,1400,1403,1405,1408],{"class":760,"line":761},[758